### Bug Description

Reloading a community package at the same filesystem path can retain an obsolete dependency entry point after the package and its dependencies have been replaced. Clearing the package's entries from `require.cache` does not fully invalidate module resolution.

Concrete case: `n8n-nodes-imap@2.17.1` uses ImapFlow 1.x (`lib/imap-flow.js`); `n8n-nodes-imap@3.0.3` uses ImapFlow 2.x (`dist/cjs/imap-flow.js`). In an isolated reproduction of n8n's unload/load mechanism, reloading the updated package tries to open the removed `lib/imap-flow.js`, even though the new package files are present and load successfully in a fresh process.

**Evidence status:**

- **Confirmed in isolation:** published IMAP node classes, sequential package replacement, the regular-package `require.cache` sweep from n8n 2.44.7, and the VM-based `require`/constructor-loading pattern reproduce the error on Node.js **22.23.1** and **24.18.0**.
- **Confirmed controls:** the same updated files load in a fresh process; a `3.0.3 → 3.0.3` reload succeeds. No IMAP server, credentials, concurrent installs, or queue workers are involved.
- **Not yet confirmed:** the complete n8n 2.44.7 UI/service update flow, rollback/database behavior, and whether this mechanism caused the original reporter's installation failure. Their exact package versions, installation history, deployment details, and full logs have been requested in [umanamente/n8n-nodes-imap#151](https://github.com/umanamente/n8n-nodes-imap/issues/151#issuecomment-6426228230). That report lists n8n 2.44.7 and the same missing entry path.

Relevant n8n 2.44.7 source:

- [DirectoryLoader.unloadAll](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/blob/n8n%402.44.7/packages/core/src/nodes-loader/directory-loader.ts#L533): sweeps `require.cache` for the package root and symlinked roots. This reproduction uses regular directories.
- [loadClassInIsolation](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/blob/n8n%402.44.7/packages/core/src/nodes-loader/load-class-in-isolation.ts#L4): VM context with the host `require`.
- [CommunityPackagesService install/update path](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/blob/n8n%402.44.7/packages/cli/src/modules/community-packages/community-packages.service.ts#L578): unloads and reloads the package after downloading the replacement.

### To Reproduce

Save the following as `repro.cjs`. It creates temporary package trees, pins the IMAP package and ImapFlow versions, installs the host API separately, loads the old node, replaces its entire package tree at the same path, and applies the cache-clearing algorithm above. Lifecycle scripts are disabled.

Run in a disposable Linux container, with network access to npm. For example, from a Bash-compatible shell:

```sh
docker run --rm -i node@sha256:16e22a550f3863206a3f701448c45f7912c6896a62de43add43bb9c86130c3e2 node < repro.cjs
```

That image ran Node.js 22.23.1. I also ran the script on Node.js 24.18.0 using `node@sha256:a0b9bf06e4e6193cf7a0f58816cc935ff8c2a908f81e6f1a95432d679c54fbfd`.

```js
const assert = require('node:assert/strict');
const fs = require('node:fs');
const os = require('node:os');
const path = require('node:path');
const { execFileSync, spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');
const { createContext, Script } = require('node:vm');

const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'n8n-community-reload-'));
const context = createContext({ require });
const results = [];
const npm = (cwd) => execFileSync('npm', [
  'install', '--install-strategy=shallow', '--legacy-peer-deps',
  '--ignore-scripts', '--no-audit', '--no-fund',
], { cwd, stdio: 'inherit' });

// n8n supplies this host API; the full n8n server is not started here.
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, 'package.json'), JSON.stringify({
  private: true, dependencies: { 'n8n-workflow': '2.28.0' },
}));
npm(root);

function stage(name, nodeVersion, imapVersion) {
  const dir = path.join(root, name);
  fs.mkdirSync(dir);
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'package.json'), JSON.stringify({
    private: true,
    dependencies: { 'n8n-nodes-imap': nodeVersion },
    overrides: { imapflow: imapVersion },
  }));
  npm(dir);
  return path.join(dir, 'node_modules/n8n-nodes-imap');
}

const oldPackage = stage('old', '2.17.1', '1.7.8');
const newPackage = stage('new', '3.0.3', '2.9.1');

function run(name, before, after, expectFailure) {
  const dir = path.join(root, 'cases', name, 'node_modules/n8n-nodes-imap');
  const entry = path.join(dir, 'dist/nodes/Imap/Imap.node.js');
  const load = () => new Script(
    `new (require(${JSON.stringify(entry)}).Imap)()`,
  ).runInContext(context);
  fs.cpSync(before, dir, { recursive: true });
  assert.equal(load().description.name, 'imap');

  // Replace the package at the same path, keeping the old tree as a backup.
  fs.renameSync(dir, dir + '.previous');
  fs.cpSync(after, dir, { recursive: true });

  // DirectoryLoader.unloadAll() sweep for a regular, non-symlink package.
  for (const key of Object.keys(require.cache)) {
    if (key.startsWith(dir)) delete require.cache[key];
  }
  const dep = path.join(dir, 'node_modules/imapflow');
  const disk = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dep, 'package.json')));
  assert.equal(disk.version, '2.9.1');
  assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(dep, 'lib/imap-flow.js')), false);
  assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(dep, 'dist/cjs/imap-flow.js')), true);

  let error;
  try { load(); } catch (caught) { error = caught; }
  if (expectFailure) {
    assert.equal(error?.code, 'ENOENT');
    assert.ok(error.message.includes('/imapflow/lib/imap-flow.js'));
  } else {
    assert.equal(error, undefined);
  }

  // Exactly the same updated files, loaded by a fresh Node.js process.
  const fresh = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['-e',
    `new (require(${JSON.stringify(entry)}).Imap)(); console.log('OK')`,
  ], { encoding: 'utf8' });
  assert.equal(fresh.status, 0, fresh.stderr);
  results.push({ case: name, node: process.version,
    hotReload: error ? error.message : 'OK', freshProcess: fresh.stdout.trim() });
}

run('2-to-3', oldPackage, newPackage, true);
run('3-to-3-control', newPackage, newPackage, false);
console.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
if (process.env.REPRO_OUTPUT) {
  fs.writeFileSync(process.env.REPRO_OUTPUT, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));
}
```

Observed final output on Node.js 22.23.1 (temporary directory name varies):

```json
[
  {
    "case": "2-to-3",
    "node": "v22.23.1",
    "hotReload": "ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/tmp/n8n-community-reload-gkCGDm/cases/2-to-3/node_modules/n8n-nodes-imap/node_modules/imapflow/lib/imap-flow.js'",
    "freshProcess": "OK"
  },
  {
    "case": "3-to-3-control",
    "node": "v22.23.1",
    "hotReload": "OK",
    "freshProcess": "OK"
  }
]
```

All assertions passed on both runtimes. The script explicitly checks that ImapFlow 2.9.1 is on disk, its new entry exists, and the old entry does not exist before the reload. The `ENOENT` is an asserted observation, so the reproducer exits successfully when it observes this behavior.

### Expected behavior

Replacing and reloading a community package should resolve dependencies using their current on-disk entry points. If a dependency transition cannot safely be reloaded in the existing process, a restart requirement should be surfaced instead of treating a valid replacement tree as missing/corrupt.

### Debug Info

This is an isolated mechanism reproduction; a full n8n server was not started, so Help → About debug information is unavailable.

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| n8n source inspected | `n8n@2.44.7`; full application update not reproduced |
| Old package / dependency | `n8n-nodes-imap@2.17.1` / `imapflow@1.7.8` |
| New package / dependency | `n8n-nodes-imap@3.0.3` / `imapflow@2.9.1` |
| Host API supplied in probe | `n8n-workflow@2.28.0`, pinned for the probe; not an assertion about the reporter's host |
| Node.js / npm | `22.23.1 / 10.9.8`; `24.18.0 / 11.16.0` |
| Operating System | Alpine Linux containers, Docker Desktop on a Windows host |
| Database | Not used in the probe; reporter's database unknown |
| Execution mode | Single sequential Node.js process; reporter's n8n mode unknown |
| Hosting | Disposable local Docker probes; reporter's hosting topology unknown |

A separate earlier probe also reproduced the transition from `2.17.0-8-gced12b5-beta` to `3.0.3`. Its resolved ImapFlow versions were also 1.7.8 and 2.9.1.

### Related reports and duplicate search

I searched open and closed issues/PRs for `require.cache`, `_pathCache`, `imap-flow.js`, module-resolution/cache terms, and community-package reload/update failures. I did not find an existing report describing this dependency-entry-point case.

- [#16072](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/16072) (merged) introduced the `require.cache` sweep. This reproduction exercises the remaining dependency-resolution state after that sweep.
- [#27106](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/27106) (closed) covers broken package files and update rollback.
- [#30533](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/30533) (closed) covers concurrent installs and stale registry/UI status. This probe is sequential and contains valid replacement files.
- Downstream reports: [#151](https://github.com/umanamente/n8n-nodes-imap/issues/151) and the earlier [#147](https://github.com/umanamente/n8n-nodes-imap/issues/147). Their shared error text is contextual evidence; the exact production cause remains unconfirmed.

### Workaround and remaining investigation

Loading the updated package in a fresh process succeeds in the isolated test. A practical workaround to validate is installing the desired version while n8n is stopped, then starting a fresh process. A failed UI update may roll back to the old package, so the actual installed version needs checking.

An earlier diagnostic probe also tried clearing matching `Module._pathCache` entries after `require.cache`; the error persisted. I am not proposing that as a complete fix. Investigation should account for all relevant resolver/package-metadata caches or use a fresh process or a loader with genuinely isolated module-resolution state, and add coverage for dependencies changing their entry paths.

The next confirmation step is an end-to-end community-package update on n8n 2.44.7, including its rollback path, plus the original reporter's diagnostics.
